  "summary": "A Francis hydraulic turbine converts the pressure and velocity of water into shaft power. Water from the penstock fills the spiral casing, passes the stay vanes and the adjustable wicket gates — which set the flow and give it swirl — and flows inward through the runner, turning it. The water leaves downward through the draft tube, which recovers energy. The vertical shaft drives a generator above.",
